+# UsdtYieldVault — pre-deployment review
+
+**Verdict: do not ship this on Monday.**
+
+Not "ship with caveats". The contract cannot take a deposit on mainnet at all: the
+first user transaction reverts against the real USDT at
+`0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7`. And if that one line were fixed, the
+next thing you'd discover is that the vault pays its depositors no yield — it is a
+0% product that charges 0.3% to leave.
+
+Nine findings below, five of them critical or high. Every one has a command and its
+verbatim output.
+
+---
+
+## How to reproduce everything
+
+Nothing under `src/` was modified. `test/UsdtYieldVault.t.sol` and `test/mocks/` are
+untouched — the original 39 tests still pass exactly as before. Everything I added is
+new files:
+
+| File | What it is |
+|---|---|
+| `test/fork/MainnetForkIntegration.t.sol` | Vault deployed against **real** USDT + **real** Aave V3 pool, forked at block 25,000,000 |
+| `test/YieldAccounting.t.sol` | Yield handling, against a pool whose aToken actually accrues |
+| `test/FeeAccounting.t.sol` | Fee handling, against the team's own `test/mocks/MockAavePool.sol` |
+| `test/AdminRisk.t.sol` | What the owner key can do to depositors |
+| `test/VaultInvariants.t.sol` | Stateful invariant testing (128,000 randomised calls) |
+| `test/VaultFuzz.t.sol` | Property-based tests |
+| `test/harness/YieldingAavePool.sol` | An aToken that rebases through a ray index, like real aUSDT |
+| `test/harness/VaultHandler.sol` | Bounded random actor for the invariant runs |
+
+The fork tests hardcode a public archive RPC (`https://eth.drpc.org`) and a pinned
+block, so `forge test` is the whole command — no env vars, no keys.
+
+Two notes on re-running, so nothing looks like it failed to reproduce:
+
+> **Invariant cache.** On a second run Foundry replays its cached counterexample and
+> prints `replay failure` instead of the values. `rm -rf cache/invariant` first for a
+> fresh run.
+>
+> **Randomised tests.** The fuzz and invariant runs use a fresh seed each time, so the
+> specific counterexample and the specific numbers in `invariant_BooksMatchTheAavePosition`
+> will differ from the ones pasted below. The pass/fail outcome is what reproduces —
+> `testFuzz_SoleDepositorEarnsYield` fails on run 0 every time, because it holds for no
+> input at all. Every other finding below is from a deterministic test with fixed
+> numbers that will match exactly.
+
+**Summary of the whole run:**
+
+```
+$ forge test --no-match-path 'test/fork/*' --no-match-contract 'VaultInvariantsTest'
+Ran 5 test suites: 43 tests passed, 12 failed, 0 skipped (55 total tests)
+```
+
+---
+
+## First, about the green tick
+
+The coverage number is real, and it is measuring the wrong thing:
+
+```
+$ forge coverage --match-path 'test/UsdtYieldVault.t.sol'
+| File                              | % Lines         | % Statements    | % Branches    | % Funcs         |
+| src/UsdtYieldVault.sol            | 100.00% (52/52) | 98.25% (56/57)  | 85.71% (6/7)  | 100.00% (11/11) |
+```
+
+100% of lines, 100% of functions. **Every single bug below lives on a covered line.**
+Line 94 — the line that makes the contract unusable on mainnet — is covered. Coverage
+proves a line was executed; it says nothing about whether anyone asserted the right
+thing about it.
+
+Three structural reasons the suite missed all of this:
+
+1. **The mocks are kinder than reality.** `MockUSDT` is a stock OpenZeppelin `ERC20`,
+   which returns `bool` from `approve`. Real USDT returns nothing. That single
+   difference is the entire gap between "39 passing" and "reverts on mainnet".
+2. **`MockAavePool`'s aToken never accrues.** It is a fixed-supply ERC20. A vault whose
+   only job is to earn Aave yield is tested against a pool that pays none, so the fact
+   that it drops 100% of the yield is invisible.
+3. **The assertions are weak where it matters.** `test_SharePriceAfterDeposit`,
+   `test_ConvertToSharesAfterDeposit`, `test_ConvertToAssetsAfterDeposit` and
+   `test_SecondDepositorMintsShares` all assert only `assertGt(x, 0)`. Those four pass
+   for almost any implementation. There are no fuzz tests, no invariant tests and no
+   fork tests in the suite.
+
+---
+
+# Findings
+
+| # | Severity | Finding |
+|---|---|---|
+| F-1 | **Critical** | `deposit` reverts against real USDT — the vault is non-functional on mainnet |
+| F-2 | **Critical** | Aave yield is never credited to anyone and is permanently stranded |
+| F-3 | **Critical** | Owner can seize an incoming deposit by front-running it with a fee spike |
+| F-4 | **High** | Exit fees are orphaned; the vault's books permanently diverge from its Aave position |
+| F-5 | **High** | Pausing freezes depositor principal; `renounceOwnership` can make that permanent |
+| F-6 | **High** | `setDepositFee` is unbounded; a fee above 100% bricks all deposits |
+| F-7 | **Medium** | Re-approving on every deposit is fragile against USDT's non-zero-allowance rule |
+| F-8 | **Low** | `aUsdt` is stored and never read; the constructor validates nothing |
+| F-9 | **Info** | The "deposit fee" is not a protocol fee and is zero for the first depositor |
+
