+
+## F-1 — Critical — `deposit` reverts against real USDT
+
+**`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:94`**
+
+```solidity
+usdt.approve(address(aavePool), amount);
+```
+
+`usdt` is typed `IERC20`, whose `approve` is declared to return `bool`. Mainnet USDT's
+`approve` returns **nothing**. Solidity emits a `returndatasize >= 32` check for the
+declared return type, so the call reverts on decode — after the user's USDT has
+already been pulled in on line 93.
+
+Note the contract uses `SafeERC20` correctly on line 93 (`safeTransferFrom`) and then
+bypasses it one line later. This is the only unguarded token call in the file.
+
+### Evidence
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path 'test/fork/MainnetForkIntegration.t.sol' -vv
+
+Ran 4 tests for test/fork/MainnetForkIntegration.t.sol:MainnetForkIntegrationTest
+[PASS] test_Fork_RealAusdtBalanceGrowsButVaultCounterCannot() (gas: 347055)
+Logs:
+  aUSDT at supply time : 99999999999
+  aUSDT after 365 days : 104072316361
+  interest accrued     : 4072316362
+  vault totalAssets()  : 0
+
+[PASS] test_Fork_RealUsdtApproveHasNoReturnValue() (gas: 37684)
+[PASS] test_Fork_RealUsdtRejectsNonZeroToNonZeroApprove() (gas: 39155)
+[FAIL: EvmError: Revert] test_Fork_UserCanDepositRealUsdt() (gas: 95873)
+Suite result: FAILED. 3 passed; 1 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 228.75ms (2.77ms CPU time)
+```
+
+The trace shows exactly where it dies — `transferFrom` succeeds, `approve` returns
+`[Stop]` (zero bytes), and the vault reverts immediately after:
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-test test_Fork_UserCanDepositRealUsdt -vvvv
+
+  [95873] MainnetForkIntegrationTest::test_Fork_UserCanDepositRealUsdt()
+    ├─ [5031] 0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7::balanceOf(alice: [0x328809Bc894f92807417D2dAD6b7C998c1aFdac6]) [staticcall]
+    │   └─ ← [Return] 100000000000 [1e11]
+    ├─ [0] VM::prank(alice: [0x328809Bc894f92807417D2dAD6b7C998c1aFdac6])
+    │   └─ ← [Return]
+    ├─ [77674] UsdtYieldVault::deposit(1000000000 [1e9])
+    │   ├─ [39630] 0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7::transferFrom(alice: [0x328809Bc894f92807417D2dAD6b7C998c1aFdac6], UsdtYieldVault: [0x5615dEB798BB3E4dFa0139dFa1b3D433Cc23b72f], 1000000000 [1e9])
+    │   │   ├─ emit Transfer(from: alice: [0x328809Bc894f92807417D2dAD6b7C998c1aFdac6], to: UsdtYieldVault: [0x5615dEB798BB3E4dFa0139dFa1b3D433Cc23b72f], value: 1000000000 [1e9])
+    │   │   └─ ← [Stop]
+    │   ├─ [24953] 0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7::approve(0x87870Bca3F3fD6335C3F4ce8392D69350B4fA4E2, 1000000000 [1e9])
+    │   │   ├─ emit Approval(owner: UsdtYieldVault: [0x5615dEB798BB3E4dFa0139dFa1b3D433Cc23b72f], spender: 0x87870Bca3F3fD6335C3F4ce8392D69350B4fA4E2, value: 1000000000 [1e9])
+    │   │   └─ ← [Stop]
+    │   └─ ← [Revert] EvmError: Revert
+    └─ ← [Revert] EvmError: Revert
+```
+
+`test_Fork_RealUsdtApproveHasNoReturnValue` isolates the mechanism: the raw call
+succeeds and returns 0 bytes, while the identical call typed as `IERC20` reverts.
+
+### Fix
+
+Use `SafeERC20`, which is already imported and already `using`-bound to `IERC20`:
+
+```solidity
+usdt.forceApprove(address(aavePool), amount);
+```
+
+`forceApprove` both tolerates the missing return value and resets the allowance to
+zero first, which also resolves F-7. Do not use `safeApprove` (removed in OZ v5).
+
