+## F-3 — Critical — Owner can seize an incoming deposit by front-running the fee
+
+**`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:84, 126-130`**
+
+`setDepositFee` takes effect in the same block, has no cap (F-6) and no timelock.
+`deposit` accepts no minimum-shares-out. The deposit fee is not swept anywhere — it
+accrues to incumbent shareholders, and the owner can be one.
+
+So: hold a token position, watch the mempool, and when a large deposit appears, front-
+run it with `setDepositFee(9_900)`. The victim's shares are minted against 1% of their
+money; the other 99% accrues to your existing shares. Then set the fee back.
+
+This requires no bug beyond the missing bound — it is a straightforward use of the
+owner's documented powers, which is what makes it worth flagging before launch rather
+than after.
+
+### Evidence
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path 'test/AdminRisk.t.sol' -vv
+
+Ran 5 tests for test/AdminRisk.t.sol:AdminRiskTest
+[FAIL: panic: arithmetic underflow or overflow (0x11)] test_DepositStillWorksAfterAnAbsurdFeeIsSet() (gas: 27696)
+[FAIL: EnforcedPause()] test_FundsCannotBeLockedForeverByPauseThenRenounce() (gas: 250870)
+Logs:
+  vault is paused    : true
+  vault owner        : 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
+  alice's locked USDT: 100000000000
+
+[FAIL: a depositor must receive ~what she paid in: 50500000000 !~= 100000000000 (max delta: 1.0000000000000000%, real delta: 49.5000000000000000%)] test_OwnerCannotSeizeAnIncomingDepositByFrontRunningTheFee() (gas: 343063)
+Logs:
+  owner stake before : 1000000000
+  owner stake after  : 50500000000
+  owner profit       : 49500000000
+  alice paid in      : 100000000000
+  alice now owns     : 50500000000
+  alice's loss       : 49500000000
+
+[FAIL: EnforcedPause()] test_PausedVaultStillLetsDepositorsExit() (gas: 238238)
+[FAIL: next call did not revert as expected] test_SetDepositFeeRejectsFeesAbove100Percent() (gas: 19389)
+Suite result: FAILED. 0 passed; 5 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 1.16ms (1.15ms CPU time)
+```
+
+A 1,000 USDT owner stake becomes 50,500 USDT in one transaction pair. Alice put in
+100,000 and owns 50,500.
+
+### Fix
+
+Defence in depth, all three:
+
+1. Cap the fee hard: `uint256 public constant MAX_DEPOSIT_FEE_BPS = 100;` (1%) and
+   `require(newFeeBps <= MAX_DEPOSIT_FEE_BPS)`.
+2. Add slippage protection: `deposit(uint256 amount, uint256 minSharesOut)` reverting
+   if `shares < minSharesOut`, and the mirror on `withdraw`.
+3. Put fee changes behind a timelock (or a `Governor`/`TimelockController` owner), so
+   a change is visible before it is live.
+
+And move the owner to a multisig — see F-5.
+
