+## F-4 — High — Exit fees are orphaned; the books diverge from the Aave position
+
+**`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:117-119`**
+
+```solidity
+totalAssetsStored -= grossAssets;          // debits the GROSS amount
+aavePool.withdraw(address(usdt), netAssets, msg.sender);   // removes only the NET
+```
+
+The fee is debited from the books but never leaves Aave and is never credited to
+anyone. It is simply dropped. The contract's own NatSpec says otherwise:
+
+> `src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:17-18` — *"Both fees stay supplied in Aave and accrue to the
+> remaining shareholders rather than being swept to the owner."*
+
+That is true of the deposit fee and false of the withdrawal fee. Since
+`totalAssetsStored` is the only input to share pricing, remaining shareholders see no
+benefit whatsoever.
+
+### Evidence
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path 'test/FeeAccounting.t.sol' -vv
+
+Ran 5 tests for test/FeeAccounting.t.sol:FeeAccountingTest
+[FAIL: vault books must match its actual Aave position: 100050025013 != 100349874937] test_BooksMatchTheAavePosition() (gas: 354630)
+Logs:
+  vault.totalAssetsStored() : 100050025013
+  aUSDT actually held       : 100349874937
+  untracked drift           : 299849924
+
+[PASS] test_Characterise_DepositFeeIsPaidToIncumbentHolders() (gas: 267073)
+Logs:
+  bob deposited                       : 100000000000
+  bob underlying immediately after    : 99949974987
+  bob's instant loss                  : 50025013
+  alice gained from bob's deposit fee : 50025012
+
+[PASS] test_Characterise_FirstDepositorPaysNoEffectiveFee() (gas: 194387)
+Logs:
+  nominal 0.1% deposit fee : 100000000
+  alice underlying         : 100000000000
+
+[FAIL: no fee may be orphaned once all shares are burned: 599999999 != 0] test_ExitFeesAreNotOrphanedAfterEveryoneLeaves() (gas: 367585)
+Logs:
+  total deposited      : 200000000000
+  shares outstanding   : 0
+  orphaned aUSDT       : 599999999
+
+[FAIL: exit fee should accrue to the remaining shareholder: 1 !~= 299849924 (max delta: 1, real delta: 299849923)] test_WithdrawFeeAccruesToRemainingShareholders() (gas: 355383)
+Logs:
+  bob's gross redemption            : 99949974987
+  exit fee bob paid                 : 299849924
+  alice underlying before bob exits : 100050025012
+  alice underlying after  bob exits : 100050025013
+  alice actually gained             : 1
+  bob received                      : 99650125063
+```
+
+Bob pays a 299.85 USDT exit fee. Alice, the only remaining shareholder, gains **1 base
+unit** — that is rounding, not the fee. Note this uses the team's own
+`test/mocks/MockAavePool.sol`, so it is independent of my harness.
+
+The invariant run finds the same drift from random call sequences, while confirming
+that solvency and share bookkeeping do hold:
+
+```
+$ rm -rf cache/invariant && forge test --match-path 'test/VaultInvariants.t.sol'
+
+[FAIL: vault books do not match its real Aave position: 1000003 != 1003203]
+[PASS] invariant_CallSummary() (runs: 256, calls: 128000, reverts: 0)
+[PASS] invariant_TotalSharesEqualsSumOfBalances() (runs: 256, calls: 128000, reverts: 0)
+[PASS] invariant_VaultIsSolvent() (runs: 256, calls: 128000, reverts: 0)
+Suite result: FAILED. 3 passed; 1 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 19.32s (48.63s CPU time)
+```
+
+**In fairness, note what passed.** Across 128,000 randomised calls I could not make the
+vault insolvent, and share bookkeeping never drifted. The drift is always in the
+depositors' favour in the narrow sense that the vault holds *more* than it thinks it
+owes. The problem is that the excess is unreachable, which is F-2's stranding problem
+by another route.
+
+(`invariant_VaultIsSolvent` carries a documented tolerance of one base unit per
+mint/burn. That dust comes from ray-index scaling in the aToken — real aUSDT included —
+not from the vault, so I excluded it rather than report it as a finding.)
+
+### Fix
+
+Decide what the fee is *for*, then make the code say so.
+
+- If it should accrue to remaining holders, as the NatSpec claims, debit only the net:
+  `totalAssetsStored -= netAssets;`. The fee then stays in Aave and raises the share
+  price for everyone left. (If you adopt F-2's fix, this becomes automatic — there is
+  no counter to debit.)
+- If it is meant to be protocol revenue, add an explicit `feeRecipient` and withdraw
+  the fee to it, or mint the equivalent shares to it.
+
+Either way, add a `test_WithdrawFeeAccruesToRemainingShareholders`-style assertion so
+the choice is pinned down.
+
