+## F-6 — High — `setDepositFee` is unbounded
+
+**`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:126-130`**
+
+No cap at all. Beyond enabling F-3, any value above `10_000` makes `amount - fee` on
+line 88 underflow, so every deposit reverts with a panic until the owner reverses it —
+a self-inflicted denial of service that a fat-fingered `setDepositFee(10001)` reaches
+immediately.
+
+### Evidence
+
+From the F-3 run above:
+
+```
+[FAIL: next call did not revert as expected] test_SetDepositFeeRejectsFeesAbove100Percent() (gas: 19389)
+[FAIL: panic: arithmetic underflow or overflow (0x11)] test_DepositStillWorksAfterAnAbsurdFeeIsSet() (gas: 27696)
+```
+
+The first shows `setDepositFee(10_001)` is accepted. The second shows the resulting
+deposit panics.
+
+### Fix
+
+```solidity
+uint256 public constant MAX_DEPOSIT_FEE_BPS = 100; // 1%
+
+function setDepositFee(uint256 newFeeBps) external onlyOwner {
+    if (newFeeBps > MAX_DEPOSIT_FEE_BPS) revert FeeTooHigh();
+    ...
+}
+```
+
+Apply the same reasoning to `WITHDRAW_FEE_BPS` if it ever becomes mutable.
+
